d #uuid "f177f9f1-b5f8-565a-af23-ef0df90fa9b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165924}] :question/id #uuid "158f6d81-386c-5243-b7cf-b10e41aa411f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96098" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3219/Source/Images/q-96098.png)\n\nWhich of the following equations could have generated the slope field shown above?\n\n1. $y^{′} = x(x - 2)$\n2. $y^{′} = \\frac{5x}{x - 2}$\n3. $y^{′} = \\frac{1}{x - 2}$"}]}
